ung 3 doesn't fit.\n  - It doesn't require parental permission. The committee version that did (\"shall obtain consent\") was replaced on the floor, so rung 5 doesn't fit either.\n- **The vote:** Koch voted Yea on final passage, roll call 345. The tally was 37–12, so this isn't a near-unanimous vote.\n- **Supporting, direction only:** Koch also voted Nay on the Yoder amendment, roll call 335. That amendment would have let a student withdraw the request so their parents wouldn't be told. Voting against it rules out the student-consent side, but on its own it doesn't pick a rung. The chair doesn't rest on it.\n\n**Judgement call:** I coded the final-passage vote `chair-shaped` (single-subject). HB 1608 also has a second section banning human-sexuality instruction from pre-K through grade 3. I treated the two sections as one subject, sex and gender in schools. If a reviewer reads the bill as multi-subject under V4.1, the Yea counts for direction only, and the row becomes BLANK `direction-only`. That's the most likely place for coders to disagree.\n\n**Other notes**\n- I recorded no quotes, because none of the sources contain Koch's own words.\n- `needs_source` is empty.\n- In the bill's operative text, `provision_quote` includes the PDF's page-break and line-number text, because the quote has to be verbatim from the snapshot.","ttft_ms":33040,"type":"result","duration_ms":56336,"uuid":"15336e82-8b4e-460f-896d-34a45f6d2302","ttft_stream_ms":1475,"time_to_request_ms":149,"first_content_frame_ms":1476,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
